1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,600
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,602 --> 00:00:03,010
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,012 --> 00:00:04,012
(Episode 75)

4
00:00:04,014 --> 00:00:06,605
I was wrong. I'm truly sorry.

5
00:00:06,634 --> 00:00:07,634
That's enough!

6
00:00:17,418 --> 00:00:18,491
Go ahead. Take a picture.

7
00:00:19,445 --> 00:00:21,381
Send it to Ji Hu.

8
00:00:21,558 --> 00:00:23,739
Tell him to let me go.

9
00:00:24,919 --> 00:00:27,191
I want to go home.

10
00:00:28,232 --> 00:00:29,598
I'm so exhausted.

11
00:00:30,552 --> 00:00:31,552
I'm sorry.

12
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:33,440
I can't watch this anymore.

13
00:00:37,145 --> 00:00:38,145
Get up.

14
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,131
You'll scrape your knees raw.

15
00:00:40,693 --> 00:00:42,500
- Let's go.
- Stay out of this.

16
00:00:46,118 --> 00:00:47,118
Come with me.

17
00:00:49,165 --> 00:00:51,144
Where are we going?

18
00:00:53,672 --> 00:00:55,058
She said, "Stay out of it."

19
00:00:56,174 --> 00:00:58,851
Do you really like that lunatic?

20
00:00:58,852 --> 00:01:01,402
You won't believe me anyway,
so why do you keep asking?

21
00:01:01,403 --> 00:01:02,483
Then what is it?

22
00:01:02,485 --> 00:01:03,772
Why are you acting this way?

23
00:01:03,945 --> 00:01:05,785
Don't you dare say you feel sorry for her.

24
00:01:05,838 --> 00:01:09,418
Do Do Hee has done countless awful things
thinking her dad would bail her out.

25
00:01:09,572 --> 00:01:12,505
Ji Hu lost his memory because of her,
and Ji Ni...

26
00:01:13,925 --> 00:01:15,163
Where do I even begin?

27
00:01:15,431 --> 00:01:18,758
Anyway, you think a staged apology
like this makes everything okay?

28
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:20,378
Then what do you want me to do?

29
00:01:21,178 --> 00:01:23,272
Should we all get in a time machine
and go back to the past?

30
00:01:23,764 --> 00:01:24,862
I'd love that.

31
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:27,112
I wouldn't have run after your car
until my legs nearly gave out...

32
00:01:28,272 --> 00:01:29,715
if I could go back.

33
00:01:30,411 --> 00:01:33,198
Why bring that up now?

34
00:01:42,385 --> 00:01:43,779
What did you buy?

35
00:01:44,176 --> 00:01:45,264
Flyers.

36
00:01:45,705 --> 00:01:48,594
I entered the wrong address,
so the package got delivered to the cafe.

37
00:01:48,882 --> 00:01:49,974
Flyers?

38
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:52,718
I heard you handed out 200.

39
00:01:53,078 --> 00:01:54,181
How did you know?

40
00:01:54,943 --> 00:01:56,849
Jung A told me.

41
00:01:57,029 --> 00:01:59,225
What are you planning to do
with those now?

42
00:01:59,785 --> 00:02:01,151
Don't worry about it.

43
00:02:01,838 --> 00:02:04,110
Are you coming home or going out?

44
00:02:04,810 --> 00:02:06,764
I stopped him from following Do Hee.

45
00:02:06,925 --> 00:02:08,898
She came to apologize.

46
00:02:09,305 --> 00:02:13,036
Her knees got scraped up,
and he's acting all heartbroken.

47
00:02:18,091 --> 00:02:19,598
That's not it.

48
00:02:26,878 --> 00:02:28,278
That little punk...

49
00:02:35,438 --> 00:02:37,229
What are these flyers for now?

50
00:02:39,638 --> 00:02:42,546
I have to get them married and move out.
I can't take this anymore.

51
00:02:55,438 --> 00:02:57,906
I'm sorry. Let me go home.

52
00:02:58,032 --> 00:03:00,122
Why didn't you apologize before
if it's this easy?

53
00:03:02,665 --> 00:03:03,722
Don't interrogate me.

54
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,961
He told me to apologize, so I came.
Now accept it.

55
00:03:07,446 --> 00:03:08,446
No.

56
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:09,945
He said he'd let me go if I apologized.

57
00:03:09,947 --> 00:03:12,078
You're only thinking about
what you want again, aren't you?

58
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:14,292
You don't even remember
what you did wrong, do you?

59
00:03:14,294 --> 00:03:16,771
Hey, just hit me.

60
00:03:17,151 --> 00:03:18,322
I'm used to taking a beating.

61
00:03:18,912 --> 00:03:22,105
I bruise easily, but the bruises
fade fast, so just hit me.

62
00:03:22,658 --> 00:03:24,085
Stop talking to me.

63
00:03:25,985 --> 00:03:28,107
Don't beat around the bush.
Tell me straight.

64
00:03:28,998 --> 00:03:29,998
You...

65
00:03:30,724 --> 00:03:32,827
What were you planning to do to me
in that storage room?

66
00:03:34,112 --> 00:03:36,069
You told those guys to kill me,
didn't you?

67
00:03:37,278 --> 00:03:39,499
Were you going to dump my body
somewhere afterward?

68
00:03:41,317 --> 00:03:43,495
Why?

69
00:03:45,305 --> 00:03:47,571
You said your mom hits you,

70
00:03:48,226 --> 00:03:52,095
so I said I struggle with mine too.
Did you hate that?

71
00:03:52,625 --> 00:03:54,769
Because I said I never knew...

72
00:03:55,814 --> 00:03:58,709
my mom like you? Did that upset you?

73
00:04:00,498 --> 00:04:02,869
Hey, stop asking.

74
00:04:03,685 --> 00:04:04,945
I still hate you.

75
00:04:05,652 --> 00:04:07,428
You have a dad and brothers,

76
00:04:08,189 --> 00:04:09,826
and a mom who's always on your side.

77
00:04:10,645 --> 00:04:12,315
Do I have to like you too?

78
00:04:13,798 --> 00:04:17,715
If I could, I'd still want to kill you.

79
00:04:18,252 --> 00:04:19,572
That's how I really feel.

80
00:04:21,274 --> 00:04:22,383
Do Do Hee.

81
00:04:23,085 --> 00:04:25,500
So accept my apology and let me go.

82
00:04:25,845 --> 00:04:28,234
I'll leave. I'll get out of your life!

83
00:04:29,251 --> 00:04:30,692
Don't come back. Ever.

84
00:04:31,445 --> 00:04:33,340
Come back after Director Cha gets married.

85
00:04:33,511 --> 00:04:35,034
And don't contact him until then.

86
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,252
Don't make Yeong Ju worry.

87
00:04:38,451 --> 00:04:39,986
You're worrying about everything.

88
00:04:41,158 --> 00:04:43,622
What if I marry Seung Woo?

89
00:04:44,548 --> 00:04:45,548
Seung Woo?

90
00:04:47,043 --> 00:04:48,417
Don't use him.

91
00:04:49,245 --> 00:04:51,817
You need someone richer and higher up.

92
00:04:51,845 --> 00:04:55,117
That's true, but we're kind of alike.

93
00:04:55,965 --> 00:04:57,677
I became this way because of you,

94
00:04:58,153 --> 00:05:00,856
and poor Seung Woo lost his dad
because of you.

95
00:05:01,831 --> 00:05:03,255
We just click.

96
00:05:03,912 --> 00:05:04,912
Enough.

97
00:05:05,529 --> 00:05:06,703
Promise me.

98
00:05:07,165 --> 00:05:08,664
Never show your face again.

99
00:05:09,465 --> 00:05:12,411
You'll let me go if I promise that, right?

100
00:05:17,752 --> 00:05:18,818
Okay.

101
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,645
Can I go now?

102
00:05:25,205 --> 00:05:26,205
Yeah.

103
00:05:38,358 --> 00:05:39,579
Dad.

104
00:05:41,149 --> 00:05:42,149
Dad.

105
00:05:44,485 --> 00:05:46,132
Is this all there is?

106
00:05:48,585 --> 00:05:50,021
This feels so hollow.

107
00:05:54,405 --> 00:05:56,061
Dad...

108
00:05:59,351 --> 00:06:01,283
What can I do...

109
00:06:03,045 --> 00:06:05,686
to ease this ache inside me?

110
00:06:29,044 --> 00:06:30,104
(How much would you like
to send to Im Ji Hu?)

111
00:06:30,105 --> 00:06:33,135
What on earth is this about
that you have to keep it from Aunt?

112
00:06:33,791 --> 00:06:36,125
This is a man-to-man conversation.

113
00:06:36,126 --> 00:06:37,206
(Would you like to transfer 20,000 dollars
to Im Ji Hu? Transfer complete)

114
00:06:44,598 --> 00:06:46,872
Uncle, why are you sending me
so much money?

115
00:06:46,873 --> 00:06:48,426
You helped us get married.

116
00:06:48,791 --> 00:06:50,578
Now it's my turn to help you get married.

117
00:06:51,915 --> 00:06:55,991
This is when I really feel that
all my hard work was worth it.

118
00:06:57,898 --> 00:06:58,965
What are you talking about?

119
00:06:58,966 --> 00:07:01,264
Use this money to plan...

120
00:07:01,812 --> 00:07:04,084
a warm, happy proposal. Then get married.

121
00:07:04,178 --> 00:07:06,998
Ji Ni isn't thinking about marriage yet.
I don't want to pressure her.

122
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,894
That's what I thought too,

123
00:07:09,081 --> 00:07:10,823
but I overheard her talking to Yeong Ju.

124
00:07:11,125 --> 00:07:13,803
Ji Ni wants to marry you too.

125
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,400
What?

126
00:07:15,845 --> 00:07:19,243
But she's embarrassed that her mom
keeps giving you a hard time,

127
00:07:19,244 --> 00:07:22,350
and most of all, she isn't confident
she can make a marriage work.

128
00:07:23,692 --> 00:07:25,098
I worry about that too.

129
00:07:25,152 --> 00:07:26,152
Exactly.

130
00:07:26,338 --> 00:07:29,216
But Yeong Ju reassured her that
you can't know until you try.

131
00:07:30,007 --> 00:07:31,693
Of course she'd worry.

132
00:07:32,191 --> 00:07:36,362
Do Hee bullied her when she was young,
and she became practically a recluse.

133
00:07:37,172 --> 00:07:39,423
Back then, the Maestro cried every day.

134
00:07:39,851 --> 00:07:41,272
I understand. I'll do my best.

135
00:07:41,345 --> 00:07:42,638
Thank you for telling me.

136
00:07:45,398 --> 00:07:46,398
Ji Ni?

137
00:07:49,758 --> 00:07:50,758
Where are you?

138
00:07:52,755 --> 00:07:53,809
What's wrong with your voice?

139
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:55,490
Have you been crying?

140
00:07:57,044 --> 00:07:58,044
Really?

141
00:07:58,806 --> 00:07:59,806
Stay right there.

142
00:08:01,498 --> 00:08:02,696
Do Hee apologized.

143
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:04,428
What a coward.

144
00:08:04,914 --> 00:08:07,658
She only did it because she's trying
to run off to England.

145
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:10,066
She's at the studio. I'll go see her.

146
00:08:10,209 --> 00:08:14,550
Wait. Take this to Ji Ni.
It's a calming herbal medicine.

147
00:08:15,598 --> 00:08:19,439
Getting an apology now
must feel pretty hollow.

148
00:08:19,441 --> 00:08:22,493
Can all those terrible things
be made right with one "I'm sorry"?

149
00:08:22,614 --> 00:08:23,728
It'll only wear her out more.

150
00:08:23,771 --> 00:08:25,128
I think she's already been crying.

151
00:08:26,271 --> 00:08:28,253
- I'll get going.
- Okay. Go check on her.

152
00:08:51,471 --> 00:08:53,759
Well? What happened?

153
00:08:53,921 --> 00:08:56,112
It's no use. They've all been bought off.

154
00:08:56,145 --> 00:08:57,842
Even her friends won't say a word.

155
00:08:58,065 --> 00:08:59,738
All they say is that
she was close to Do Hee.

156
00:09:00,503 --> 00:09:01,711
Those awful people.

157
00:09:01,998 --> 00:09:04,787
They say Do Hee's father
is a big shot in politics.

158
00:09:05,272 --> 00:09:06,405
What about you?

159
00:09:06,618 --> 00:09:08,263
Don't you know anyone who could help?

160
00:09:08,511 --> 00:09:10,941
Ask your father in Seo Chon.

161
00:09:11,005 --> 00:09:13,875
The people we know don't stand a chance
against them.

162
00:09:14,072 --> 00:09:15,767
So we're just going to give up?

163
00:09:15,845 --> 00:09:18,110
How can she get by
as a middle school dropout?

164
00:09:20,271 --> 00:09:21,736
We have to save our child first.

165
00:09:21,738 --> 00:09:24,958
That's why I told you
to get the paperwork done first.

166
00:09:25,245 --> 00:09:28,288
How did you let things get to this?

167
00:09:29,997 --> 00:09:34,192
- Se Ri.
- What about my poor Ji Ni?

168
00:09:42,145 --> 00:09:43,197
Honey.

169
00:09:46,345 --> 00:09:48,419
Do Hee came and apologized.

170
00:09:50,049 --> 00:09:51,502
Ji Hu made it happen.

171
00:09:53,985 --> 00:09:55,084
But...

172
00:09:57,351 --> 00:09:59,054
I have mixed feelings.

173
00:10:00,172 --> 00:10:01,390
What is all this?

174
00:10:02,511 --> 00:10:05,968
Is everything just going to be buried?

175
00:10:14,498 --> 00:10:15,599
You did the right thing.

176
00:10:16,352 --> 00:10:18,914
It may seem unfair,
but you've freed yourself.

177
00:10:20,805 --> 00:10:24,537
Storage rooms won't scare you anymore.
Neither will seeing Do Hee.

178
00:10:26,006 --> 00:10:27,570
Do you really think so?

179
00:10:29,183 --> 00:10:30,683
Aunt said...

180
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:34,103
as long as she held on to her resentment
toward your mom,

181
00:10:34,948 --> 00:10:36,656
she was trapped in a prison herself.

182
00:10:38,745 --> 00:10:41,556
Let your prisoner go
and set yourself free too.

183
00:10:43,285 --> 00:10:45,953
It's not that easy to change how I feel.

184
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:47,924
I know.

185
00:10:51,591 --> 00:10:53,608
Excuse me. I need to take a call.

186
00:10:54,592 --> 00:10:56,266
My phone keeps vibrating.

187
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:00,401
My mom?

188
00:11:02,692 --> 00:11:04,795
- Ji Hu.
- I told you not to do this.

189
00:11:05,643 --> 00:11:07,986
So he is with you?

190
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:09,539
Okay.

191
00:11:10,804 --> 00:11:11,928
Ji Ni.

192
00:11:12,061 --> 00:11:13,061
What?

193
00:11:14,478 --> 00:11:16,178
This must be hard on you.

194
00:11:17,052 --> 00:11:18,929
I'm thinking of your dad too.

195
00:11:19,645 --> 00:11:21,891
Don't let your thoughts overwhelm you.

196
00:11:22,044 --> 00:11:24,130
Just think of happy things with Ji Hu.

197
00:11:24,605 --> 00:11:28,070
Ji Hu stepped in for your dad
and got you an apology from Do Hee.

198
00:11:30,327 --> 00:11:32,354
Okay. Goodbye.

199
00:11:37,545 --> 00:11:40,118
See? No one cares as your mom does.

200
00:11:51,505 --> 00:11:53,608
Why does everyone look so worn out?

201
00:11:54,351 --> 00:11:55,351
Did something happen?

202
00:11:56,358 --> 00:11:57,893
Yeong Ju, is something wrong?

203
00:11:58,493 --> 00:11:59,836
- Worrying about my son...
- It's my son.

204
00:12:02,172 --> 00:12:03,294
What's wrong with your son?

205
00:12:03,296 --> 00:12:05,661
What about you? What's wrong with Ji Hu?

206
00:12:06,125 --> 00:12:09,067
I'd happily raise ten sons like Ji Hu.

207
00:12:09,955 --> 00:12:11,047
Aunt.

208
00:12:12,932 --> 00:12:16,566
I'll make you something nourishing.
And some for you too, honey.

209
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,051
- No, there's no need...
- No, it's okay...

210
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:32,559
Won't you come to the clinic?

211
00:12:33,039 --> 00:12:35,072
I can't. I'm sorry.

212
00:12:35,538 --> 00:12:37,245
I could divorce you over this.

213
00:12:38,111 --> 00:12:40,741
- What?
- When I proposed to you,

214
00:12:40,768 --> 00:12:42,590
you were so cheerful, Yeong Ju.

215
00:12:43,285 --> 00:12:44,884
And what did I tell you?

216
00:12:45,132 --> 00:12:48,398
Stop running after your sons
and grandson, and be with me.

217
00:12:48,578 --> 00:12:52,242
I said I'd make you happy again
as a woman, Yeong Ju.

218
00:12:54,581 --> 00:12:57,455
- So?
- Ever since we got married,

219
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,384
it's always been about your sons.

220
00:13:00,034 --> 00:13:01,895
We can't even enjoy married life.

221
00:13:03,238 --> 00:13:06,110
Stop sulking and go to work.

222
00:13:06,112 --> 00:13:07,185
No Yeong Ju.

223
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,327
- What?
- Sulking?

224
00:13:11,405 --> 00:13:13,404
I may be younger than you,

225
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,407
but am I your little brother?
How is this sulking?

226
00:13:16,918 --> 00:13:19,426
I'm nice, so I always say, "Okay,"

227
00:13:19,428 --> 00:13:21,498
or "Whatever you want."
Does that make me a fool?

228
00:13:21,955 --> 00:13:23,776
What's gotten into you?

229
00:13:23,778 --> 00:13:25,912
Seung Woo is a grown man.

230
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:27,235
Whoever he's dating,

231
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:30,463
you married me, so focus on me.

232
00:13:30,552 --> 00:13:31,977
You're lying here,

233
00:13:32,185 --> 00:13:35,230
wondering where Seung Woo is
every 30 minutes.

234
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:38,428
Is that how you treat the man
you chose to share your life with?

235
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:40,334
Rest and think about that.

236
00:13:40,668 --> 00:13:41,726
Sa Bin.

237
00:13:41,772 --> 00:13:44,476
You said you didn't mind
if I was tone-deaf,

238
00:13:44,543 --> 00:13:46,465
as long as I wasn't life-deaf.

239
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:49,297
Now you're life-deaf.

240
00:13:49,338 --> 00:13:51,427
You miss every note and every beat.

241
00:13:51,487 --> 00:13:54,570
You've forgotten who you live with
and where you live!

242
00:14:01,105 --> 00:14:02,269
Uncle.

243
00:14:12,678 --> 00:14:14,827
Uncle, what's wrong?

244
00:14:15,545 --> 00:14:19,735
It's the only way I can save her
from all this.

245
00:14:20,232 --> 00:14:23,191
Otherwise, she'll stay trapped
in an endless cycle of worry.

246
00:14:24,132 --> 00:14:27,446
It's not like we can lock Seung Woo up.

247
00:14:28,212 --> 00:14:29,506
Do Hee is leaving soon.

248
00:14:29,892 --> 00:14:31,844
I certainly hope so.

249
00:14:31,868 --> 00:14:33,451
Then we can finally have some peace.

250
00:14:33,672 --> 00:14:35,677
That's all I'm waiting for too.

251
00:14:36,487 --> 00:14:37,487
I'll go.

252
00:14:46,964 --> 00:14:49,300
- Welcome.
- Hello.

253
00:14:51,198 --> 00:14:52,198
Ma'am.

254
00:14:52,223 --> 00:14:53,478
Hello, Jung A.

255
00:14:57,108 --> 00:14:58,831
So you're the owner.

256
00:14:59,048 --> 00:15:01,461
I had no idea. I thought you didn't work.

257
00:15:01,486 --> 00:15:03,428
I'd rather do this than stay home.

258
00:15:03,978 --> 00:15:04,993
What was your job again?

259
00:15:05,018 --> 00:15:06,764
I teach at an art academy.

260
00:15:06,789 --> 00:15:09,879
Your feet must get sore a lot.

261
00:15:09,904 --> 00:15:11,333
Choose a pair.

262
00:15:15,698 --> 00:15:17,192
I know this brand.

263
00:15:17,472 --> 00:15:20,890
My mom wears these shoes
with every outfit.

264
00:15:20,915 --> 00:15:23,630
Your mom has good taste.

265
00:15:23,654 --> 00:15:25,707
They're on me.
Pick out a pair for your mom too.

266
00:15:25,732 --> 00:15:27,899
Ma'am, you're the best!

267
00:15:29,078 --> 00:15:32,062
You're so friendly.

268
00:15:32,152 --> 00:15:33,152
Listen,

269
00:15:33,176 --> 00:15:35,460
be that nice to Ji Hu too.

270
00:15:37,089 --> 00:15:38,089
Okay?

271
00:15:40,778 --> 00:15:41,778
Okay.

272
00:15:52,898 --> 00:15:54,203
Guess who?

273
00:16:00,999 --> 00:16:01,999
What?

274
00:16:03,389 --> 00:16:04,389
I...

275
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:07,019
took your side
even when my mom, my brother,

276
00:16:07,709 --> 00:16:09,972
and even Ji Ni's family...

277
00:16:10,115 --> 00:16:11,584
criticized me for it.

278
00:16:11,828 --> 00:16:14,643
- You know that, right?
- I do. Thank you.

279
00:16:17,578 --> 00:16:19,692
So what are you going to do now?

280
00:16:19,992 --> 00:16:22,561
Did you give Ji Ni a proper apology?

281
00:16:22,586 --> 00:16:23,702
Of course.

282
00:16:23,772 --> 00:16:25,473
She said she'd forgive me.

283
00:16:25,872 --> 00:16:28,013
I've settled everything from my past.

284
00:16:28,037 --> 00:16:29,037
I did a good job, right?

285
00:16:29,938 --> 00:16:32,889
So you're going to England now?

286
00:16:33,531 --> 00:16:35,924
Director, I really can't thank you enough.

287
00:16:35,948 --> 00:16:36,948
Should I give you a kiss?

288
00:16:37,872 --> 00:16:40,956
Do Do Hee,
why do you act this way with me?

289
00:16:41,232 --> 00:16:42,956
How do you feel about me?

290
00:16:43,452 --> 00:16:45,409
Always hugging me and clinging to me.

291
00:16:48,359 --> 00:16:49,470
Do you like me?

292
00:16:49,572 --> 00:16:51,375
That's what I wanted to ask you.

293
00:16:52,272 --> 00:16:53,272
Director,

294
00:16:53,603 --> 00:16:55,236
don't you actually like me?

295
00:16:55,818 --> 00:16:58,594
Who does all this just out of pity?

296
00:16:58,751 --> 00:17:00,196
So...

297
00:17:00,886 --> 00:17:04,314
you act this way
because you think I like you?

298
00:17:04,766 --> 00:17:07,580
- Don't you?
- That's because I...

299
00:17:07,656 --> 00:17:08,951
have a big heart.

300
00:17:09,192 --> 00:17:10,399
It doesn't matter.

301
00:17:10,838 --> 00:17:12,383
I'm going to leave anyway.

302
00:17:12,645 --> 00:17:14,595
Ji Ni agreed to forgive me,

303
00:17:14,619 --> 00:17:16,716
but only if I stopped seeing you.

304
00:17:17,405 --> 00:17:19,324
She said I could return
once you're married.

305
00:17:19,858 --> 00:17:22,348
She's so protective of you.
Since when were you her brother?

306
00:17:24,385 --> 00:17:26,811
Besides, I don't want to be family
with Ji Ni either.

307
00:17:28,195 --> 00:17:30,396
- What?
- Even if I avoided her, we'd be family.

308
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:33,862
I'd have to see Ji Ni and Ji Hu
living happily together, wouldn't I?

309
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:34,887
No way.

310
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:38,589
And my family wouldn't even consider
someone like you.

311
00:17:38,952 --> 00:17:41,142
We're best as we are, right?

312
00:17:44,589 --> 00:17:45,600
Cha Seung Woo.

313
00:17:45,624 --> 00:17:48,058
- You! Again?
- Stop!

314
00:17:48,285 --> 00:17:49,695
It's not what you think.

315
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,689
This is just our last goodbye.

316
00:17:52,204 --> 00:17:54,634
Please don't hit me anymore.

317
00:18:02,491 --> 00:18:03,491
Bye.

318
00:18:11,165 --> 00:18:12,408
Come to your senses.

319
00:18:12,584 --> 00:18:14,584
You're chasing her all on your own?

320
00:18:15,458 --> 00:18:17,660
It's not like that.

321
00:18:22,814 --> 00:18:24,274
That's my ring!

322
00:18:25,332 --> 00:18:28,466
I knew it.
I knew she was the one who took it.

323
00:18:29,652 --> 00:18:30,831
Now you see what she's like.

324
00:18:30,948 --> 00:18:34,338
She stole my wedding ring.
Do you understand?

325
00:18:34,915 --> 00:18:36,231
I understand.

326
00:18:36,518 --> 00:18:38,246
She's leaving for England anyway.

327
00:18:38,772 --> 00:18:39,932
I won't see her again.

328
00:18:40,593 --> 00:18:41,745
Honestly...

329
00:18:42,063 --> 00:18:45,739
You're just like your dad.
You're both poor judges of character.

330
00:18:45,763 --> 00:18:48,540
You're all heart and no brains.

331
00:18:48,542 --> 00:18:49,658
Mom!

332
00:18:49,994 --> 00:18:52,016
You know I hate hearing that.

333
00:18:57,865 --> 00:18:58,865
Seriously!

334
00:19:14,631 --> 00:19:15,741
Yes, perfect.

335
00:19:19,876 --> 00:19:23,116
Am I doing this right?
I've never played a wizard before.

336
00:19:23,141 --> 00:19:25,038
You're doing great.

337
00:19:27,108 --> 00:19:28,944
- Want to take a look?
- Is that okay?

338
00:19:28,969 --> 00:19:30,010
Okay.

339
00:19:32,665 --> 00:19:35,062
This is amazing.

340
00:19:35,158 --> 00:19:36,784
When will my face start appearing?

341
00:19:36,808 --> 00:19:37,899
Starting next week.

342
00:19:37,924 --> 00:19:40,771
By the way, can you act?

343
00:19:41,596 --> 00:19:44,554
"Act?" I've never tried.

344
00:19:44,864 --> 00:19:46,871
Though my whole life has been an act.

345
00:19:47,806 --> 00:19:51,486
We're actually discussing making
a short-form drama based on this game.

346
00:19:52,048 --> 00:19:54,614
Would you mind if I recommended you?
Would you like to give it a try?

347
00:19:54,884 --> 00:19:57,562
If I get to play a wizard, I'm in.

348
00:19:57,587 --> 00:19:58,930
Sounds fun.

349
00:19:59,771 --> 00:20:01,467
Shall we head to the recording studio?

350
00:20:01,738 --> 00:20:03,603
- Sure.
- This way.

351
00:20:07,616 --> 00:20:09,654
- Hello.
- Welcome.

352
00:20:09,687 --> 00:20:11,193
Did you just open this place?

353
00:20:11,405 --> 00:20:13,030
Yes, I just moved here.

354
00:20:13,055 --> 00:20:15,410
But my mom and I ran this place
for years, about 20 years ago.

355
00:20:15,435 --> 00:20:18,018
- I've come back to it.
- Really?

356
00:20:18,218 --> 00:20:19,891
I've lived around here all my life too.

357
00:20:21,192 --> 00:20:22,259
A long time ago,

358
00:20:22,283 --> 00:20:25,369
do you remember an accident
in the alley behind here?

359
00:20:25,394 --> 00:20:27,262
The child who was hit by a motorcycle?

360
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:29,142
Yes, that's the one.

361
00:20:29,798 --> 00:20:33,136
Please contact me
if you remember anything.

362
00:20:33,878 --> 00:20:35,721
And could I leave these...

363
00:20:36,418 --> 00:20:39,034
by the entrance for guests to take?

364
00:20:39,211 --> 00:20:42,556
So you're her son.

365
00:20:43,272 --> 00:20:45,092
Your mom doesn't like this.
You should stop.

366
00:20:45,276 --> 00:20:46,276
What?

367
00:20:47,065 --> 00:20:48,065
My mom?

368
00:20:48,498 --> 00:20:49,566
Do you know my mom?

369
00:20:49,591 --> 00:20:51,859
You should think about her too.

370
00:20:52,941 --> 00:20:56,154
How upsetting it must be for her to see
you obsess over this instead of working.

371
00:20:56,191 --> 00:20:57,564
My mom said that?

372
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,454
Yeah. She even ordered rice cakes.

373
00:21:04,845 --> 00:21:05,845
This woman?

374
00:21:06,542 --> 00:21:08,152
No, not her.

375
00:21:08,838 --> 00:21:11,771
The woman was taller, like a model.

376
00:21:15,619 --> 00:21:17,038
Was it this woman?

377
00:21:17,313 --> 00:21:20,748
That's her! Isn't she your mom?

378
00:21:33,265 --> 00:21:34,265
Who do we have here?

379
00:21:34,554 --> 00:21:38,172
My goodness! Look who's here!

380
00:21:38,305 --> 00:21:40,591
Is this really my daughter, Na Ji Ni?

381
00:21:44,078 --> 00:21:47,600
- Does it look weird?
- No, you're so pretty.

382
00:21:47,624 --> 00:21:49,227
My goodness!

383
00:21:49,252 --> 00:21:51,519
I kept telling you to wear skirts,

384
00:21:51,543 --> 00:21:53,519
but you insisted on doing kicks.

385
00:21:54,025 --> 00:21:57,962
Ji Hu really is working miracles
left and right.

386
00:21:58,006 --> 00:22:01,642
- You look pretty.
- Mom, you're overdoing it.

387
00:22:02,631 --> 00:22:03,747
I'm not.

388
00:22:03,772 --> 00:22:05,480
Ji Hu says he's almost here.

389
00:22:05,677 --> 00:22:07,803
Hey, can I come along too?

390
00:22:08,278 --> 00:22:10,287
I want to see Ji Hu too.

391
00:22:17,232 --> 00:22:18,642
Are you my mom?

392
00:22:19,023 --> 00:22:20,123
What are you talking about?

393
00:22:20,148 --> 00:22:23,017
Why are you pretending to be my mom
and keeping a witness quiet?

394
00:22:23,292 --> 00:22:24,860
What are you really up to?

395
00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:27,908
Where did you hear such nonsense?
What are you going on about?

396
00:22:27,932 --> 00:22:29,898
What's going on? What did my mom do?

397
00:22:29,932 --> 00:22:32,996
The woman from the rice cake shop
came forward as a witness,

398
00:22:33,011 --> 00:22:35,057
but your mom told her the case was closed.

399
00:22:35,197 --> 00:22:37,861
She said she was my mom...

400
00:22:37,885 --> 00:22:39,560
and that there was no need
to look for the culprit!

401
00:22:40,218 --> 00:22:42,593
Can you believe she did that
while I'm handing out these flyers?

402
00:22:43,043 --> 00:22:44,043
Does that make any sense?

403
00:22:44,305 --> 00:22:45,685
Well...

404
00:22:45,710 --> 00:22:48,364
Did you know about this too?

405
00:22:49,454 --> 00:22:50,454
Yeah.

406
00:22:50,791 --> 00:22:54,455
So that's why you acted as if you knew
the owner of the rice cake shop last time?

407
00:22:55,324 --> 00:22:57,048
- Are you two running a scam together?
- Hey!

408
00:22:57,049 --> 00:22:59,098
You think you can say whatever you want?

409
00:22:59,145 --> 00:23:00,927
Ji Ni knew nothing about it.

410
00:23:00,952 --> 00:23:04,803
And I had my suspicions
when that foolish woman came by too.

411
00:23:04,848 --> 00:23:07,967
So I questioned her thoroughly,
but she didn't know a thing.

412
00:23:07,992 --> 00:23:11,654
So I told her the case was closed
and not to come back.

413
00:23:11,738 --> 00:23:15,013
I was afraid you'd be disappointed again
or get ripped off again!

414
00:23:15,015 --> 00:23:16,679
Even if I get ripped off,
that's my problem!

415
00:23:16,932 --> 00:23:18,776
Why did you step in and change the story?

416
00:23:19,538 --> 00:23:21,935
I don't know what's going on,
but please calm down.

417
00:23:21,937 --> 00:23:23,087
Stay out of this.

418
00:23:23,592 --> 00:23:25,416
Don't get involved
when you don't know anything.

419
00:23:26,295 --> 00:23:29,451
Seung Hyun, I understand why you're upset.

420
00:23:30,631 --> 00:23:33,020
I don't know if I should say this,

421
00:23:34,013 --> 00:23:35,710
but I feel guilty too.

422
00:23:35,970 --> 00:23:37,516
That's why I got involved.

423
00:23:37,692 --> 00:23:39,498
I was there
when the accident happened too.

424
00:23:39,778 --> 00:23:42,616
I'm upset that
I couldn't protect Seung Woo either.

425
00:23:43,068 --> 00:23:44,068
Pumseongak.

426
00:23:45,398 --> 00:23:47,604
No one has ever mentioned
anything that specific.

427
00:23:48,091 --> 00:23:51,758
I heard they told you too.
So why did you say she knew nothing?

428
00:23:51,945 --> 00:23:54,879
You know I've been searching
everywhere for even the smallest clue.

429
00:23:54,903 --> 00:23:56,185
Why would you hide this from me?

430
00:23:56,209 --> 00:23:58,939
- I'm sorry, but...
- What could you possibly be hiding...

431
00:23:58,964 --> 00:24:01,453
- by pretending you're my mom?
- That's not what this is about!

432
00:24:01,572 --> 00:24:02,907
Then what was I supposed to say?

433
00:24:02,932 --> 00:24:05,236
Your second mom?

434
00:24:05,571 --> 00:24:07,985
You're making a big deal out of nothing!

435
00:24:08,509 --> 00:24:10,320
Mom, please stop.

436
00:24:11,220 --> 00:24:12,327
I'm sorry.

437
00:24:12,745 --> 00:24:14,377
Don't ever pull something like this again.

438
00:24:18,353 --> 00:24:19,353
That little...

439
00:24:25,511 --> 00:24:26,511
Ji Hu,

440
00:24:26,575 --> 00:24:28,628
marry her soon so we can move out.

441
00:24:28,911 --> 00:24:31,261
- This is giving me a headache.
- Yes, Mother.

442
00:24:35,091 --> 00:24:38,088
Hey, Ji Ni! Where are you going?

443
00:24:38,112 --> 00:24:40,592
Why go back in there
just to get yelled at again?

444
00:24:45,652 --> 00:24:48,173
I'm sorry. My mom was out of line.

445
00:24:49,106 --> 00:24:50,106
Forget it.

446
00:24:50,131 --> 00:24:53,716
I should've looked into it myself,
but I just took my mom's word for it.

447
00:24:54,024 --> 00:24:56,673
She called her a scammer,
so I believed her.

448
00:24:56,772 --> 00:24:58,273
I shouldn't have done that.

449
00:24:58,923 --> 00:24:59,923
Please leave.

450
00:25:20,872 --> 00:25:22,381
I'm so embarrassed.

451
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:26,148
Why do I keep showing you this side of me?

452
00:25:27,012 --> 00:25:31,299
I wish I'd been born into a normal family.

453
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,030
Ji Ni.

454
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:36,166
I'm jealous of Jung A.

455
00:25:37,185 --> 00:25:38,826
She has both her parents,

456
00:25:39,710 --> 00:25:42,462
and she graduated college without
going through anything unusual.

457
00:25:44,678 --> 00:25:46,116
That's just how I feel.

458
00:25:47,324 --> 00:25:49,433
No one knows how much I envy...

459
00:25:49,850 --> 00:25:54,091
how easily she can talk about her family.

460
00:26:01,925 --> 00:26:04,458
You once said everyone has a shadow
as big as they are.

461
00:26:05,339 --> 00:26:06,546
Don't compare yourself to others.

462
00:26:08,477 --> 00:26:10,022
You remember that?

463
00:26:10,985 --> 00:26:14,445
I wrote that for a contest
before my dad passed away.

464
00:26:16,234 --> 00:26:19,825
I told you how hard it was for me
to carry my own shadow too.

465
00:26:20,997 --> 00:26:23,026
Sometimes, I'd look in the mirror
and wonder.

466
00:26:23,811 --> 00:26:25,521
What did my dad look like?

467
00:26:27,445 --> 00:26:29,175
At least I got to see my mom.

468
00:26:31,272 --> 00:26:32,681
I'd look at my own face...

469
00:26:33,511 --> 00:26:35,511
and try to imagine
what my dad looked like.

470
00:26:36,159 --> 00:26:39,652
Not knowing where you come from
is a very lonely feeling.

471
00:26:41,163 --> 00:26:42,369
Ji Hu.

472
00:26:45,078 --> 00:26:46,701
Let's build a family of our own.

473
00:26:48,745 --> 00:26:50,926
Our kids will know
what their parents look like,

474
00:26:51,570 --> 00:26:53,766
and they'll be able to say,
"We're just a normal family."

475
00:27:20,132 --> 00:27:21,586
I'll be an ordinary husband.

476
00:27:23,172 --> 00:27:25,394
I'll give you a happy, comfortable life.

477
00:27:26,924 --> 00:27:28,427
A life filled with peace and security.

478
00:27:31,512 --> 00:27:32,512
Will you...

479
00:27:34,029 --> 00:27:35,120
marry me?

480
00:27:48,631 --> 00:27:49,710
Thank you.

481
00:28:51,265 --> 00:28:54,363
(Family Register)

482
00:28:54,365 --> 00:28:56,738
It's barely been a month
since I asked for more time,

483
00:28:56,762 --> 00:28:58,189
and now you're telling me you proposed?

484
00:28:58,191 --> 00:29:00,290
You're just using that time
to find a way to reject Ji Ni.

485
00:29:00,315 --> 00:29:01,923
Ji Ni hasn't done anything wrong.

486
00:29:01,948 --> 00:29:03,637
Put your prejudice aside and support her.

487
00:29:03,639 --> 00:29:04,908
Guess you'll miss me when I'm gone.

488
00:29:04,933 --> 00:29:06,002
I wish I could leave too.

489
00:29:06,027 --> 00:29:08,394
You said you'd never like her.
So why are you chasing after her?

490
00:29:08,409 --> 00:29:09,842
Mother, please accept me.

491
00:29:09,877 --> 00:29:12,204
Your fault?
You were never meant to be born.

492
00:29:12,229 --> 00:29:14,150
Ji Ni, my mom left home.

493
00:29:15,976 --> 00:29:17,976
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
